"entity": {
"name": "BioMarin Pharmaceutical Inc.",
"description": "BioMarin Pharmaceutical, Inc. is a global rare disease biotechnology company focused on delivering medicines for people living with genetically defined conditions. The company has a proven track record of innovation, with nine commercial therapies and a strong clinical and preclinical pipeline. Using a distinctive approach to drug discovery and development, BioMarin seeks to unleash the full potential of genetic science by pursuing category-defining medicines that have a profound impact on patients. The company was founded by John C. Klock, Christopher M. Starr and Grant W. Denison on March 21, 1997 and is headquartered in San Rafael, CA.",
